  "riskClass": "medium",
  "title": "CompliancePage upload handler uses FormData but passes it to authFetch which may add wrong Content-Type",
  "description": "R6 deep audit finding. Dimension: Wiring. Severity: P2. Source SHA: bbd487a3. Scope: R6_DEEP_AUDIT_WAVE. In handleUpload, the code creates a FormData object and sends it via `authFetch('/api/v1/retailer-admin/compliance', accessToken, { method: 'POST', body: formData })`. The authFetch wrapper (api.ts line 76) correctly skips setting Content-Type for FormData bodies (the browser auto-sets the multipart boundary). However, the formData variable name shadows the component state: the form data object is named `formData` (line 93) while the component also uses `setFormData` pattern from other pages. This is confusing but works because CompliancePage doesn't have a state variable named formData. The actual concern is that the endpoint path '/api/v1/retailer-admin/compliance' is used for POST but the file is not uploaded using the documents API (`/api/v1/documents/upload`) that the registration flow uses - this may be a different endpoint entirely.",
